    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493309528/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """Thursday, Oct. 18, 1906
Fine.
Logan’s 40th birthday.
Alys and Logan came up.Karin still sick from chloroform.
Mozart and Wagner [at] Queen’s Hall.
B.B. at Nîmes.
Friday, Oct. 19, 1906
X.
Fine.
Karin better. Appetite coming back.
Nina called. Spragues etc. sent flowers.
B.B. at Montpellier.
Saturday, Oct. 20, 1906
Fine.
Karin much better. We began “Vanity Fair”. She  is  a plucky creature.
B.B. at Toulouse (Sète, Pésenas, Béziers, Narbonne) Carcassonne
Sunday, Oct. 21, 1906
Fine.
Karin much better. All goes well - Even the dressing didn’t hurt.
B.B. at Rodez.
London"""^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 127 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1906> .

